      "_doc": "0.33 п.9: what a press of a watched event entity is — by its HA device class, else by words of its event type / name (a SIP call of an intercom integration has no doorbell class). One push per press, its words by kind; «sos» is critical (through silent mode and quiet hours).",
      "sos": {"words": "(?<![a-z])sos(?![a-z])|panic|emergency|паник|тревожн|экстренн"},
      "doorbell": {"classes": ["doorbell"], "words": "doorbell|(?<![a-z])ring|incoming|(?<![a-z])call|intercom|(?<![a-z])sip(?![a-z])|звон|вызов|домофон"}
    },
    "ring_push": {
      "_doc": "Р55: a doorbell's push — the door's picture (a camera of the same device, the talk camera skipped), a tap opens the dashboard view with the door, time-sensitive (iOS) / high (Android) unless quiet hours or critical. «Answered» (the agent's intercom state, a SIP integration's event type) takes the push off every phone; a hang-up / an ended or answered call is no push of its own (a missed call keeps the ring's push).",
      "kinds": ["doorbell"],
      "skip_camera_keys": ["intercom_talk"],
      "ios": {"interruption-level": "time-sensitive"},
      "android": {"priority": "high", "ttl": 0, "importance": "high"},
      "clear_states": ["talking", "answered_elsewhere"],
      "clear_event_types": ["connected", "answered", "answered_elsewhere", "talking"],
      "skip_event_types": ["ended", "hangup", "hang_up", "hung_up", "cancelled", "canceled", "rejected", "missed", "idle"]
    },
